                <pb facs="0562" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/933: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-05T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1919, 4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 5, 2.07
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1990. Commission’s 1772, April 24, 7 p.m. Peretti informs us that in conformity
                    with our conversation with him instructions were issued to Fardet, the new
                    French Receiver in Liberia, to suspend his departure from France, but that it
                    has just been ascertained that he left on April 8.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
